From 3fe3315184936cfa9c310f5e87b1ba15bbf78cf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kuzma30 <kuzemkoa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:09:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/24] Modeling Algorithms - Fillet a square hole edge by
 edge, corner patches on spheres

FreeCAD issue 20085, a cube of 20 with fillets of radius 6 and a square
hole of 8 x 8 whose walls go along the tangent lines of the fillets of
the cube:
- an upper edge of the hole filleted, then the next one in a second
  operation: "command not done";
- all edges given (the option of FreeCAD to use all edges): one corner
  of the hole turned inside out.

- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformCapInSectionPlane: the second fillet stops at
  the end of the first one, where its spine goes on along the tangent
  edge between the wall and the sphere of the corner of the cube, on
  which the ball does not fit any more. Its last section lies in the
  plane of the next wall, through the vertex where it stops. The end is
  closed by a planar cap in that plane, bounded by the section, by the
  arc of the section through the vertex and by the line from the vertex
  to the other end of the section. The cap is a corner of the fillet
  ending at the vertex.
- ChFi3d_Builder::ComputeOnce: a face of the result whose wire goes
  twice through a vertex (two parts of the wall touching at the corner
  of the cap) is split into one face per part.
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformFilletOnVertex: at the other end of the second
  fillet, the walking went on past the vertex along the extension of the
  spine, with one side out of its face. When the last surfdata on two
  faces ends on two arcs through the vertex, the surfdatas after it are
  removed, and the end is computed as for a single fillet.
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformIntersectionAtEnd: such surfdatas at the other
  end of the stripe are not counted as pieces of the fillet; with them
  the end was closed by a corner patch (tolerance 1.8 with r = 2.25 for
  three of the four upper edges filleted alone). A missing face is not
  used to check the tangency of the faces around the vertex (a crash).
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformMoreThreeCorner: the boundary of a corner patch
  on a face is a batten computed in the parameters of the surface. On a
  sphere it depended on the axis of the sphere, and two of the spheres
  of the corners of the cube have a horizontal axis: the patch of one
  corner was turned inside out. On a sphere the batten is computed for
  the sphere whose axis goes through the vertex of the corner.

A second upper edge next to a filleted one: the 12 ordered pairs are
valid for r = 0.5 to 2.9 with tolerance 2.1e-4 at most, and each fillet
removes the same volume (2.3110 mm3 with r = 1, 14.1751 mm3 with r = 2).
A single upper edge gives the same volume for the four edges up to
r = 2.9. All edges with r = 2: the center of gravity is on the axis of
the hole within 7e-5 (2.2e-3 before), tolerance 0.079 (0.102 before).

The splitting of a face touching itself at a vertex also makes the
results of the tests blend simple H8 and blend buildevol D8 (OCC22817)
valid: their TODO is removed. The concave fillet of the start wall of
the FreeCAD screw (issue 32486) is now built with r = 0.02 and 0.05 to
0.07 too.

New DRAW tests bugs/modalg_8/fillet_rounded_cube_square_hole_second_fillet
and bugs/modalg_8/fillet_rounded_cube_all_edges_symmetric, GTests
BRepFilletAPI_MakeFilletTest.SquareHoleInRoundedCube_SecondFilletNextToFirst
and BRepFilletAPI_MakeFilletTest.SquareHoleInRoundedCube_AllEdgesCornersAlike.

